Sum(Take(Map(1..oo, _ => _^2), 10))

// JS: the infinite array is an issue. We should materialize the Take on an infinite collection.
// ((((_f) => (Array.from({length: Infinity}, (_e, i) => 1 + i)).map((_x) => _f(_x)))(((_) => (_ * _)))).slice(0, Math.max(0, 10))).reduce((_a, _b) => _a + _b, 0)


/// ## Auto-Map


1..oo |> Take(_, 10) |> Map(_, _^2) |> Sum


// The following should be equivalent:
// 1..oo |> Take(10) |> x => x^2 |> Sum
// 1..oo |> Take(10) |> _^2 |> Sum

// Note: 1/ The `Take` operator has an implicit `_` as its first argument, when compatible, 2/ when the rhs of `|>` is a lambda with a shape compatible with `Map(_, ...)` the `Map` is implicit. 3/ In that case the `_` is a marker for an implicit lambda argument (that might be ambiguous...)


// $\sum_{i=1}^{10} i^2$



